<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Paris bans protests after violent unrest as Macron takes swipe at Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6b9cad45ed5e7f648423aae8337afc9cb116beae3eb068eefbc9446c5d08628</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T02:28:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump" /><summary type="html">French police banned protests in parts of Paris on Thursday as authorities braced for further demonstrations following some of the worst street unrest in years. The restrictions came after President Emmanuel Macron appeared to accuse US President Donald Trump of exploiting the violence for political gain ahead of US midterm elections. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian missiles hit Kyiv as Moscow signals readiness for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658d85892b185e21f46e45dd8e0f7f96094c2516c2d0a958464f2b975bdd840e</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T01:51:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-russia-missiles-kyiv-ukraine-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Russian missiles struck Kyiv overnight, wounding six people and forcing residents into shelters, Ukrainian authorities said Thursday, hours after Moscow signalled readiness to resume US-mediated peace talks. President Donald Trump said negotiations were closer than ever to ending the war, though the Kremlin expressed doubts over Ukrainian and European proposals.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland votes to end UN approval requirement for overseas peacekeeping missions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c7deee5f595c8058ee8e20137ebe4f446b93adeae2e668676efb682655fc488</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T00:35:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-ireland-votes-un-veto-overseas-peacekeeping-missions" /><summary type="html">Irish lawmakers voted Wednesday to scrap a requirement for UN approval before deploying military peacekeepers overseas, approving the controversial legislation by 79 votes to 71. Opposition lawmakers warned the move threatened Ireland’s longstanding military neutrality. Ireland is not a NATO member but has traditionally participated in international peacekeeping missions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Real Madrid thrash RB Leipzig as Mbappe scores in Champions League win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5474b4c994147ac05b6d3f119baa44e19408320fcbe1563697f00cb92bb2e14f</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T00:11:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261022-real-madrid-thrash-rb-leipzig-as-mbappe-scores-in-champions-league-win" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid thrashed RB Leipzig 4-1 on Wednesday to secure their third consecutive Champions League victory. Bernardo Silva, Arda Guler, Kylian Mbappe and Yan Diomande scored for Jose Mourinho’s side, while Tidiam Gomis replied for Leipzig. Mbappe has scored in all three European matches this season, taking his tally to 12 goals.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan’s war escalates as UN warns of wider regional crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97e7949e083e6175529d5d0abb484995ef565c4411f98a90aa00a2f0bf0256a3</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:41:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis" /><summary type="html">In tonight’s edition: Sudan’s brutal war continues to take a devastating regional toll, as a drone strike in Abyei reportedly kills 153 people. We speak to the UN envoy for Sudan following an emergency international meeting on the escalating crisis. Also, health authorities prepare to coordinate a response as Ebola cases emerge in Nigeria and rise in Kenya. Finally, ten years after Cameroon’s deadliest railway disaster, families of the 79 victims are still fighting for justice, saying their pain has yet to be acknowledged.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin 'destroying' US democracy with 'autocratic, terrorist version of Christian nationalism'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:188fcb980dd5d122f4be7a1ebf375255d69deb59142dfe0b79f77d0ade4af06a</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:11:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-nationalism" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes former US Assistant Secretary of Defense Jim Townsend and former US Air Force officer Michael (Mikey) Weinstein, founder and president of the Military Religious Freedom Foundation. Is American military power becoming an instrument of political and religious coercion, both at home and abroad? From the reported restrictions on Ukraine's access to Starlink satellite communications to the Trump administration's overtures towards Vladimir Putin and the growing controversy over religious ideology within the Pentagon, the two guests offer a stark assessment of the direction of American foreign and defence policy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV needs no further lung cancer treatment, Vatican says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa4c0ed1be9ecbf74fdf5eed2368b7ad3247fd24772d1c671e3827cdfae593c0</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T21:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-pope-leo-doctors-treatment-lung-cancer" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV, 71, will require no further treatment for lung cancer after tests confirmed the disease was localised, the Vatican said Wednesday. The pontiff underwent surgery last week to remove part of his right lung after being diagnosed with adenocarcinoma. He was discharged Saturday and will gradually resume activities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>In run-up to mass protests and riots, pro-Russian accounts amplified French anger, NGO finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6c07123424ff35b0156235cfbb4c7953c8889493adf4b99fba7989afae9ee69</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T21:25:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261021-in-run-up-to-mass-protests-and-riots-pro-russian-accounts-amplified-french-anger-ngo-finds" /><summary type="html">Research carried out by the Alliance4Europe NGO suggests that pro-Russian networks manipulated information online in an effort to exacerbate anger in France ahead of last weekend's massive protests and subsequent unrest. After analysing more than half a million posts across various social media platforms, the group says it was able to track the campaign back to the start of September. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Omri Preiss, Managing Director at the Alliance4Europe.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>In run-up to mass protests and riots, pro-Russian accounts amplified French anger, NGO finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:004c1248762e92e219872d41e66a1ff2de7c3142bb5849d28040b99d57c9bcfe</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T21:21:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-run-up-to-mass-protests-and-riots-pro-russian-accounts-amplified-french-anger-ngo-finds" /><summary type="html">Research carried out by the Alliance4Europe NGO suggests that pro-Russian networks manipulated information online in an effort to exacerbate anger in France ahead of last weekend's massive protests and subsequent unrest. After analysing more than half a million posts across various social media platforms, the group says it was able to track the campaign back to the start of September. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Omri Preiss, Managing Director at the Alliance4Europe.</summary></entry><entry><title>Meta fined $25 billion in New Mexico over Cambridge Analytica scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:557519aeee5113836d9f703cee9ac84840dceb1a364b52e68b8bc5d265d67cc4</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T21:21:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261021-meta-fined-25-billion-new-mexico-cambridge-analytica-scandal" /><summary type="html">A New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25 billion after a jury found the company deceived users in a case linked to the Cambridge Analytica scandal, media reported Wednesday. The ruling follows an $18 billion settlement with 48 other states over similar claims. Meta called the penalty “a tax on speech.”</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>French bond yields hit 24-year high after unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:425104731b614c06b84937cbe2d875dfe8c13c24cabd04fe306f044f47ba1ef4</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T20:43:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-bond-yields-hit-24-year-high-after-unrest" /><summary type="html">French bond yields have topped 5%, their highest level since 2002, after widespread protests and violence over the weekend. It's a sign that investors are losing confidence in France's finances, as the government grapples with budget and debt problems. Also in the show - chipmaker Nvidia says it's invested $10 billion in European tech firms to boost the 'AI economy,' and the UK approves a controversial natural gas field as PM Andy Burnham faces pressure over energy costs.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right group</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0055fd2deee0bcbce86d0aab77b714e5ea5e086767ee6b9cdab1b6e95f61800f</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T20:21:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-group" /><summary type="html">The far-right European Parliament group of French presidential frontrunner Marine Le Pen's party said Wednesday EU prosecutors were searching its offices as part of a graft probe into its now-defunct predecessor. The Patriots for Europe group said the European Public Prosecutor's Office (EPPO) had been searching its administrative offices in Brussels and Strasbourg "since this morning".  FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Strasbourg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin agrees to resume three-way talks with Kyiv and Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5594b9999853c7683a5e3e5e0f04bb4b0e4097768b782defda115540928bc58</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/putin-agrees-to-resume-three-way-talks-with-kyiv-and-washington" /><summary type="html">President ⁠Volodymyr Zelenskiy ​said on Wednesday ​that Ukraine supported a US proposal for ​three-way talks ‌with Russia ⁠and the United ‌States at the level ⁠of negotiators to be held as soon ​as possible, preferably ‌no later than early November. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe, Russia and Eurasia Programme at Chatham House, says that "it's not clear whether Putin would meet Trump and Zelensky", adding that "meeting Zelensky is the last thing that Putin would be prepared to do".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adda69676c0076cd346a9ff0feed6356a4b02688f203ef114d9e26e24e90831f</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making “stupid comments” at France’s expense. Trump’s focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8383eaf5d5f8a9e6fa61a72cb523c314d8b82146eedf7cb9a71a3b502e5667ee</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war" /><summary type="html">The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".</summary></entry><entry><title>Le Pen sees polls boost amid mass protests, riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:996e4173a0d4cc6cbbc7e1827122ef90e4ee4c4f7bd4dc20332a3fb1375066e4</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T18:56:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-sees-polls-boost-amid-mass-protests-riots" /><summary type="html">Marine Le Pen is set to officially launch her presidential campaign this weekend at the National Rally two-day party congress in Orléans. The latest Ifop poll, carried out in the wake of the mass protests and riots in France, suggests the far right leader would win the first round of the presidential election by a wide margin, and far-left candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon emerged as her most likely opponent in the runoff. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump faces fresh questions over ties to 'humanitarian' Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fee72e0e5e8a92e781226757bd72bb5dde0df67629d86cb25f26983b43f3a28f</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T18:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-faces-fresh-questions-over-ties-to-humanitarian-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's pivot away from Ukraine has triggered fresh questions about his attachment to Russian leader Vladimir Putin, the man a top American envoy flattered on Wednesday as a "humanitarian. Trump has cast his dealings with Putin as part of a mega-deal that has secured the release of American detainee Stephen Hubbard -- and which Trump says will end Russia's war on Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canadian publisher drops author Orelien after confirming he used AI in debut novel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b56a0465b91e1cab87682c788261d7c03eaf09de69cdce2ebbf01cdc43bd41f0</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T17:32:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261021-canadian-publisher-drops-author-orelien-after-confirming-he-used-ai-in-debut-novel" /><summary type="html">The Canadian publisher representing Thélyson Orélien on Wednesday said it had dropped the prize-nominated writer over new information indicating that he did use artificial intelligence to write his acclaimed debut.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Riyadh to show solidarity amid Houthi attacks, ease tensions at home via fuel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3e9719d97d25d245340297d4c0ca8cef86d151df1a04f085176d9a41b86ea48</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T17:09:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-riyadh-show-solidarity-amid-houthi-attacks-ease-tensions-home-via-fuel-deal" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Wednesday paid an unannounced visit to Riyadh in a bid to underscore French support for the kingdom amid intensified attacks by Houthi rebels and an attempt to ease tensions at home by securing oil and diesel imports.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Greece: Protesters draw inspiration from demonstrations in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a0b9a68a7925ed0b9eafe02a03e2bba1b7ee74f226e9f516211da48f79e1d55</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:31:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-greece-protesters-draw-inspiration-from-demonstrations-in-france" /><summary type="html">Inspired by protests in France and other parts of Europe, thousands of Greek students on Wednesday demonstrated around the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>World set to breach 1.5°C warming limit set by Paris Climate Agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64684a20cff4eda008468a33b27c5a060aae995d7e229aec2508c100a1aaffb2</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-world-set-to-breach-1-5%C2%B0c-warming-limit-set-by-paris-climate-agreement" /><summary type="html">The UN is warning that global commitments to cut planet-heating emissions are falling far short of the Paris climate goals of 1.5 degrees Celsius warming – and put the world on course for 2.6C warming this century. The report by the United Nations Environment Programme lays bare the chasm between rhetoric and action when it comes to tackling global warming, and the challenge before political leaders at November's COP31 climate summit - set to take place next month in Turkey. Story by Emerald Maxwell.</summary></entry><entry><title>French President Macron lands in Saudi Arabia on surprise 'solidarity' visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:248d125dd7475e51b7fea0872c19cd54bd4772d8b52c09396ba3233c0cb1b518</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-president-macron-lands-in-saudi-arabia-on-surprise-solidarity-visit" /><summary type="html">⁠French President Emmanuel ​Macron landed in Riyadh on Wednseday, ‌adding an ⁠unscheduled stop to his ‌ongoing tour of the Gulf ⁠region. The president's office said the visit aimed to demonstrate “France's solidarity” ​with Saudi Arabia in ‌the face of attacks launched by the ‌Houthis against its territory. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says 'ready' to resume 3-way talks with US and Ukraine mid-November</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b047110d8b4fece8ead8945869c5765e8c31299bde7d145727eef726843e25a</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:51:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kremlin-says-ready-to-resume-3-way-talks-with-us-and-ukraine-mid-november" /><summary type="html">Moscow is ready to resume trilateral US-Ukraine-Russia talks next month, the Kremlin said Wednesday after President Vladimir Putin met with US envoy Steve Witkoff in Russia. FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron rejects Trump’s claims blaming migrants for French riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d65ed63472bb8001b3bfb8841d4e0dc2ff15d68f1c1f039578c95de7ce9be9</id><updated>2026-10-22T05:03:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-macron-rejects-trump-s-claims-blaming-migrants-for-french-riots" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron condemned comments by "foreign leaders" on the violent protests in France on October 17. He has now arrived in Saudi Arabia as part of his Gulf tour.</summary></entry></feed>
